<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iwakura Mission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871–1873</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iwakura Mission was a Japanese embassy that toured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from 1871 to 1873, led by Iwakura Tomomi with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kido-takayoshi">Kido Takayoshi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okubo-toshimichi">Ōkubo Toshimichi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi">Itō Hirobumi</a>. It failed to revise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unequal-treaties">unequal treaties</a>, but it studied Western government, industry, education and military systems, and its findings shaped the modernising reforms of the Meiji government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iwakura-mission.jpg" alt="Iwakura Mission" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iwakura_mission.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
